This 64-bit OS is coded in C89 and is made to, as of now, only run in Class 3
machines—machines that can only boot in UEFI, not BIOS unlike Class 2 or
Class 1 machines.

It is currently made to boot from a (properly formatted) USB device and is only
made for x86-64 Intel CPUs—though it is made to run on only one CPU (the BSP).